---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import FeatureItem from '../components/FeatureItem.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="b-oss - blipfoto - open source software"
  description="b-oss makes small, focused desktop tools. Currently home to b-ark, a local backup app for blipfoto."
  nav="home"
>
  <Hero label="Hero" icon="b-oss" title="Open source tools for blipfoto.">Free to download, use, modify or build on.</Hero>

  <section class="block" data-screen-label="About b-oss">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">About</p>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 18px">
      <p style="">
        <b>b-oss</b>&nbsp;= Blipfoto - Open Source Software<br />Open source means anyone can
        see the source code, build the software themselves, modify it, and contribute
        improvements back. If you have the skill and the interest, you can join the development
        team.
      </p>
      <p>
        b-oss was started by <strong>Ian Stevenson</strong> — a technologist with thirty years'
        experience as a software engineer and running software companies — using Claude Code and
        other AI tools for implementation. Ian is also one of the directors of blipfoto, but
        b-oss is a personal project and has no formal relationship with blipfoto.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="app-card" data-screen-label="App: b-ark">
    <div class="app-card-meta">
      <div class="app-card-head">
        <img src="assets/b-oss-icon.png" alt="" />
        <div>
          <h2>b-ark : Backup & Archive</h2>
          <div class="tagline">Archive your blips on your own device (Windows).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">
        b-ark makes a local copy of every blip you've ever posted (images, text and metadata) on
        your own machine, automatically keeping it up to date. Browse offline, publish to the
        web, or hand over to AI tools to explore and create new formats.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <FeatureItem><strong>Backup.</strong> A local copy of every blip, updated automatically.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>View.</strong> Browse your archive offline in the built-in viewer.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>Publish.</strong> Copy the backup folder to any web host to publish.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>AI-ready.</strong> README.md for AI tools: Use AI to build photobooks,
            slideshows, statistics, custom sites.</FeatureItem>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="b-ark.html">Learn more →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shot" aria-label="b-ark screenshot">
      <img
        src="assets/b-ark-screenshot.png"
        alt="The b-ark app showing an account with archived photos."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="app-card" data-screen-label="App: b-mobile">
    <div class="app-card-meta">
      <div class="app-card-head">
        <img src="assets/b-oss-icon.png" alt="" />
        <div>
          <h2>b-mobile : Blipfoto for Android</h2>
          <div class="tagline">Browse, post and get notified from your phone.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">
        A Blipfoto app for Android: browse everything, post a blip from your camera or gallery,
        join in with stars, favourites and comments, and choose whether to be notified.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="b-mobile.html">Learn more →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="app-card" data-screen-label="App: b-api">
    <div class="app-card-meta">
      <div class="app-card-head">
        <img src="assets/b-oss-icon.png" alt="" />
        <div>
          <h2>b-api</h2>
          <div class="tagline">TypeScript client for the Blipfoto v4 REST API.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="summary">
        b-api is the HTTP client that b-ark is built on. It covers the full Blipfoto v4 REST API
        and it works in browsers, Node.js 18+, and Electron alike. Clone the b-oss repository
        and import b-api directly into your TypeScript project.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <FeatureItem><strong>TypeScript.</strong> Full types for every request, response, and error. No
            guessing.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>Universal.</strong> No Node or Electron dependency. Works in browsers,
            Node.js 18+ and Electron.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>Complete.</strong> Journals, entries, CRUD, comments, social, OAuth,
            notifications, user settings.</FeatureItem>
        <FeatureItem><strong>Error-safe.</strong> Typed <code>BlipfotoError</code> and
            <code>NetworkError</code> with helpers for rate limits and token expiry.</FeatureItem>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn primary" href="b-api.html">Learn more →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shot" aria-label="b-ark screenshot">
      <img
        src="assets/b-api-screenshot.png"
        alt="The b-ark app showing an account with archived photos."
      />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
